<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-11-13T10:15:35+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:15:35 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Researchers on 28 Peruvian cacao farms found birds and bats nearly doubled harvests by pest control]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135757943.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A recent study highlights the vital role of wildlife, particularly birds and bats, in managing pests on cacao farms. These creatures enhance cacao production, especially in areas rich in trees, leading to improved farmer profits. However, for farmers to maximize these benefits, preserving diverse habitats and effectively managing tree growth to ensure adequate light for cacao trees is essential.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/researchers-studying-28-peruvian-cacao-farms-found-that-trees-attracting-birds-and-bats-nearly-doubled-harvests-through-pest-control-adding-an-estimated-1640-per-hectare-in-yearly-production-value-/articleshow/135757943.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/researchers-studying-28-peruvian-cacao-farms-found-that-trees-attracting-birds-and-bats-nearly-doubled-harvests-through-pest-control-adding-an-estimated-1640-per-hectare-in-yearly-production-value-/articleshow/135757943.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T09:52:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135758031,imgsize-201314.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A dead star called J1328-1450 is circled by two separate rings of shattered planets]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135756245.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a groundbreaking discovery, astronomers have identified two unique gaseous rings encircling the white dwarf star J1328-1450. Utilizing the Very Large Telescope in Chile, researchers explored the surrounding materials, indicating that some smaller planetary bodies likely survived the star's catastrophic end. Unlike previous findings, these rings display varied chemical compositions, shedding light on the planetary conditions that existed prior to the star's demise.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/a-dead-star-called-j1328-1450-is-circled-by-two-separate-rings-of-shattered-planets-unlike-any-seen-before-and-astronomers-say-it-hints-at-what-may-survive-when-our-sun-dies-billions-of-years-from-now/articleshow/135756245.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/space/a-dead-star-called-j1328-1450-is-circled-by-two-separate-rings-of-shattered-planets-unlike-any-seen-before-and-astronomers-say-it-hints-at-what-may-survive-when-our-sun-dies-billions-of-years-from-now/articleshow/135756245.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T09:47:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135756245,imgsize-163604.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[DC gym shooting: Shooter complained about mould, water damage in apartment before attacking]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135787466.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Shooting incidents occurred in a Washington DC gym where Dr. Matt Lambert opened fire, killing the building manager. Witnesses described scenes of chaos and horror during the attack. Lambert had expressed grievances over issues in his apartment prior to the shooting. He had been involved in a lawsuit against the condominium association regarding alleged damages. The shooting ended with Lambert taking his own life after a police standoff.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/shooter-complained-about-mould-water-damage-in-apartment-before-attacking-washington-dc-gym/articleshow/135787466.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/shooter-complained-about-mould-water-damage-in-apartment-before-attacking-washington-dc-gym/articleshow/135787466.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T08:50:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135787816,imgsize-304964.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump backed Huang till end, urged him to fight for job amid China spy scandal]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135786217.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[US President Donald Trump urged Nvidia co-founder Jensen Huang to fight to retain his job shortly before his exit amid a China spy scandal, NYT reported. Trump continued backing Huang despite intelligence warnings about his alleged affair with a Chinese woman suspected of spying for Beijing. Bloomberg reported that Huang later called Trump and expressed remorse over the scandal's impact on his family.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-backed-nvidias-jensen-huang-till-end-urged-him-to-fight-for-job-amid-spy-scandal-report/articleshow/135786217.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-backed-nvidias-jensen-huang-till-end-urged-him-to-fight-for-job-amid-spy-scandal-report/articleshow/135786217.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T07:23:42+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Abhishek Mishra</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135786242,imgsize-1099184.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Well done, specialist': Hegseth honours soldier who scolded his team at war memorial]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135785477.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth presented Specialist Thomas Iglesias with the Joint Service Commendation Medal for his actions. This award was given for reminding officials to maintain silence and respect at the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier on Veterans Day. Iglesias's reprimand of Hegseth and aides was captured in a video widely shared on social media.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/well-done-specialist-pete-hegseth-awards-medal-to-soldier-who-scolded-his-team-at-war-memorial/articleshow/135785477.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/well-done-specialist-pete-hegseth-awards-medal-to-soldier-who-scolded-his-team-at-war-memorial/articleshow/135785477.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T06:09:38+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135785528,imgsize-1112385.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Colorado contractor jailed for stealing $1.4 million from homeowners]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135755388.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-colorado-home-remodelling-contractor-stole-more-than-1-4-million-from-homeowners-and-abandoned-projects-after-demolition-he-has-been-sentenced-to-10-years-in-prison/articleshow/135755388.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-colorado-home-remodelling-contractor-stole-more-than-1-4-million-from-homeowners-and-abandoned-projects-after-demolition-he-has-been-sentenced-to-10-years-in-prison/articleshow/135755388.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T08:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135755606,imgsize-1974296.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida woman who lived quietly for 23 years leaves $4 million fortune to charity]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135756905.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-woman-who-lived-quietly-in-a-rented-apartment-for-23-years-leaves-4-million-fortune-to-a-food-bank-and-animal-services-giving-each-organisation-2-million/articleshow/135756905.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/florida-woman-who-lived-quietly-in-a-rente