/articleshow/135781533.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T01:07:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Poulomi Ghosh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135781688,imgsize-91770.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Montana Supreme Court rules 10 extra driving miles aren't enough to change a father's custody plan]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135743986.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Montana Supreme Court has reaffirmed a previous ruling on a parenting plan modification initiated by Justin Aikins, who sought changes after his ex-wife moved a mere 10 miles away. The court concluded that minor increases in distance do not justify altering existing custody arrangements. Attempts at mediation were unsuccessful, and this decision establishes an important precedent regarding relocations and shared parenting in Montana.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-montana-father-sought-to-change-his-parenting-plan-after-his-former-wife-moved-arguing-it-made-visits-harder-the-state-supreme-court-ruled-that-10-extra-driving-miles-were-not-enough-to-reopen-the-arrangement/articleshow/135743986.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-montana-father-sought-to-change-his-parenting-plan-after-his-former-wife-moved-arguing-it-made-visits-harder-the-state-supreme-court-ruled-that-10-extra-driving-miles-were-not-enough-to-reopen-the-arrangement/articleshow/135743986.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T05:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135745971,imgsize-1415422.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A London financier lost his £2.6 million claim to his mother's Chelsea home]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135762603.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/london-financier-spent-over-20-years-living-in-his-mothers-3-85-million-chelsea-home-before-demanding-a-2-6-million-share-judge-rejected-his-claim-and-ordered-him-to-pay-85000-annually/articleshow/135762603.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/london-financier-spent-over-20-years-living-in-his-mothers-3-85-million-chelsea-home-before-demanding-a-2-6-million-share-judge-rejected-his-claim-and-ordered-him-to-pay-85000-annually/articleshow/135762603.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T04:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135762746,imgsize-1606770.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Oklahoma homeowner fined $8,528 as Supreme Court restores ban on his short-term rental business]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135746069.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A recent ruling by the Supreme Court has imposed a hefty fine of over $8,000 on an Oklahoma homeowner, Adewale Eniola Tawose. This decision reinstates the community's ban on short-term rentals after a legal tussle. Tawose's attempts to host guests led the homeowners association to act against him, reversing an earlier judgment that allowed his rental business, thus affirming the penalties and restrictions on such properties.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-oklahoma-homeowner-hosted-141-guests-during-36-short-term-stays-despite-neighbourhood-rules-after-a-lower-appeals-court-lifted-restrictions-the-state-supreme-court-restored-the-ban-and-upheld-8528-in-fines/articleshow/135746069.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-oklahoma-homeowner-hosted-141-guests-during-36-short-term-stays-despite-neighbourhood-rules-after-a-lower-appeals-court-lifted-restrictions-the-state-supreme-court-restored-the-ban-and-upheld-8528-in-fines/articleshow/135746069.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T04:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135746250,imgsize-2273507.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[An endangered leatherback turtle tried to nest on an Ecuador sidewalk before finding a quieter beach]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135716561.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Bella, a resilient leatherback turtle, made a remarkable nesting attempt in Ecuador, overcoming an array of challenges posed by artificial lighting. Her successful hatchling rates reveal a promising trend, indicating that leatherbacks are beginning to adapt to their new coastal environments. Conservation efforts are increasingly vital as these turtles face persistent threats, highlighting the urgent need to establish safe habitats for their upcoming nesting seasons.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/critically-endangered-leatherback-turtle-bella-makes-remarkable-nesting-attempts-in-ecuador-achieving-918-hatch-success-rate/articleshow/135716561.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/nature/critically-endangered-leatherback-turtle-bella-makes-remarkable-nesting-attempts-in-ecuador-achieving-918-hatch-success-rate/articleshow/135716561.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-13T03:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135716895,imgsize-1014011.cms"/></item></channel></rss>